# Legacy static-file URLs from before /about and /privacy were prerendered
# Angular routes. Kept as explicit 301s (not a catch-all) so any old
# bookmarks or indexed links land on the real, current page instead of a
# 404. Do not add a "/* ... 200" catch-all here again — that's what made
# every nonexistent URL return a soft-200 in the first place. Cloudflare's
# not_found_handling ("404-page" in wrangler.jsonc) is what returns a real
# 404 for anything not covered by a real file or one of the rules below.
/about.html    /about    301
/privacy.html  /privacy  301
/author        /author/henri-evjen  301
